slave: a refused TIOCSCTTY is fine when the pty already is the controlling terminal (QNX)

QNX makes a terminal the controlling terminal of a session leader that
opens it (System V behaviour), so after setsid() and open() of the pty slave
it already is, and ioctl(TIOCSCTTY) then fails with EPERM. foot treated that
as fatal: the shell was never started ("failed to configure controlling
terminal: Operation not permitted"). On QNX accept the refusal when the pty
is this session's terminal already (tcgetsid() == getsid(0)), as the vte
port does.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/slave.c
+++ b/slave.c
@@ -240,7 +240,14 @@
         goto err;
     }
 
-    if (ioctl(pts, TIOCSCTTY, 0) < 0) {
+    if (ioctl(pts, TIOCSCTTY, 0) < 0
+#if defined(__QNX__)
+        /* QNX has already made the pty the controlling terminal when it
+         * was opened after setsid(), and then refuses TIOCSCTTY (EPERM):
+         * not a failure */
+        && tcgetsid(pts) != getsid(0)
+#endif
+        ) {
         LOG_ERRNO("failed to configure controlling terminal");
         goto err;
     }
